  "caption": "Quinn's watch kept beeping \"180!\", so Quinn ran with tiny steps — and soon the calves were on fire.\n\nKay's take: 180 steps a minute came from watching elite racers. Cadence follows your speed and stride, so there's no universal number. A small increase from your own baseline may ease some knee pain, but it shifts load to the calf and Achilles. \n\nWhat can help: measure your own rate, nudge it up only a few percent, get guidance rather than relying on watch alerts, and build calf strength — it may feel harder for a few weeks.\n\nGet it checked for sudden calf or Achilles pain, a tender spot on a bone, night pain, swelling, or knee pain lasting around two months.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
